Package: functai
Title: Functions Whose Body a Language Model Writes, for the Tidyverse
Version: 0.1.0
Authors@R: person("Maxime", "Rivest", email = "maxime.rivest@gmail.com", role = c("aut", "cre", "cph"))
Description: Write a function's inputs, its answer's type and a sentence
    saying what it does; a language model writes the body. The functions
    are vectorised, so they work as columns in 'dplyr' verbs; the answer
    comes back as the type you declared (a factor, a number, a tibble of
    fields). Measure how often a function is right with a confidence
    interval ('broom'-style tidy(), glance() and augment()), log every call,
    rate calls, improve functions with worked examples, and run functions
    saved in 'Python' or 'TypeScript'. Implements the same contract as the
    'Python' and 'TypeScript' packages.
License: MIT + file LICENSE
URL: https://github.com/MaximeRivest/functai, https://maximerivest.github.io/functai/
BugReports: https://github.com/MaximeRivest/functai/issues
Encoding: UTF-8
Depends: R (>= 4.1.0)
Imports: cli, curl, generics, lm15 (>= 1.0.0), lmcc (>= 0.8.4), openssl,
    rlang (>= 1.1.0), stats, tibble, utils, vctrs (>= 0.6.0), withr
Suggests: dplyr, httpuv, testthat (>= 3.0.0), tidyr
